PEAK TOTAL (sum of per-component peaks): 2329 MiB = 2.27 GiB

Budget: ~4 GB. Headroom: ~1.7 GB.

TWO_NODE=1 adds a fifth JVM (loan-application node B), another ~360 MiB by
the figure above, for ~2.7 GiB total -- still inside the budget.

Largest single consumer is Kafka at 656 MiB against its 1g mem_limit (64%).
No container came close to its limit; the tightest ratio after Kafka is
Grafana at 131/512 MiB.

